---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Source">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Open by default</span>
    <h1>Read the code behind every score.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      GameBench is not a black-box ranking site. The game briefs, browser tests,
      scoring rules, clean model-made source, and published result records are public.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button" href="https://github.com/Carrick-K7/carrick-ai-gamebench">Open GitHub</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/methodology">Understand the score first</a>
    </div>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="grid cols-3">
        <article class="card">
          <span class="pill">Game rules</span>
          <h3>What every model receives</h3>
          <p>Starter code, game briefs, public state shapes, browser checks, time limits, seeds, and point values.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="pill">Scorekeeper</span>
          <h3>How the browser awards points</h3>
          <p>Real input, controlled time, game-state checks, build gates, clean rebuild verification, and score aggregation.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <span class="pill">Model output</span>
          <h3>What you can download</h3>
          <p>Playable builds, screenshots, licenses, and clean source—with credentials, private model traces, and provider responses removed.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section prose">
      <h2>What you may reuse</h2>
      <p>
        GameBench code is Apache-2.0. Reproduce tasks retain their upstream
        license, exact commit, copyright notices, and distributed-material
        hashes. A published file never broadens the license of upstream work.
      </p>
      <h3>Site typefaces</h3>
      <p>
        The interface self-hosts Oxanium, Silkscreen, Smiley Sans, and Fusion
        Pixel under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. The exact
        {" "}<a href="/fonts/licenses/Oxanium-OFL.txt">Oxanium</a>,
        {" "}<a href="/fonts/licenses/Silkscreen-OFL.txt">Silkscreen</a>,
        {" "}<a href="/fonts/licenses/SmileySans-OFL.txt">Smiley Sans</a>, and
        {" "}<a href="/fonts/licenses/FusionPixel-OFL.txt">Fusion Pixel</a>
        {" "}license texts ship with the site.
      </p>
      <h2>Why games open on another domain</h2>
      <p>
        Model-generated JavaScript is untrusted. Every game runs on an isolated
        play domain with outside network access disabled and no access to the
        main site's cookies, storage, or page.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
